    "objects": {
      "general": [
        {
          "properties": {
            "paragraphs": [
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "What are the 225?",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontFamily": "'Inter SemiBold', 'Segoe UI Semibold', wf_segoe-ui_semibold, helvetica, arial, sans-serif",
                      "fontSize": "8pt",
                      "color": "#1F2328"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "Occupations: kinds of jobs with an official title and code, like Registered Nurses or Accountants and Auditors, not 225 positions. 202 are named jobs and 23 are “all other” groups, such as “Managers, All Other”. About 1.4M people work in them in NYC (2025, our estimate).",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontFamily": "Inter, 'Segoe UI', wf_segoe-ui_normal, helvetica, arial, sans-serif",
                      "fontSize": "8pt",
                      "color": "#1F2328"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": " ",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontFamily": "Inter, 'Segoe UI', wf_segoe-ui_normal, helvetica, arial, sans-serif",
                      "fontSize": "4pt",
                      "color": "#5B6470"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "Who picked them?",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontFamily": "'Inter SemiBold', 'Segoe UI Semibold', wf_segoe-ui_semibold, helvetica, arial, sans-serif",
                      "fontSize": "8pt",
                      "color": "#1F2328"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "No one, by hand. The U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics (BLS) rates each of its 831 occupations by the schooling it usually takes to start (2025–35 projections). The 225 are every one it rates associate's (48) or bachelor's (177): the whole list, not a sample.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontFamily": "Inter, 'Segoe UI', wf_segoe-ui_normal, helvetica, arial, sans-serif",
                      "fontSize": "8pt",
                      "color": "#1F2328"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": " ",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontFamily": "Inter, 'Segoe UI', wf_segoe-ui_normal, helvetica, arial, sans-serif",
                      "fontSize": "4pt",
                      "color": "#5B6470"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "Are they all of NYC's degree jobs?",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontFamily": "'Inter SemiBold', 'Segoe UI Semibold', wf_segoe-ui_semibold, helvetica, arial, sans-serif",
                      "fontSize": "8pt",
                      "color": "#1F2328"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "All of them by that rule, which is strict: it goes by what new workers need, not what workers hold. In 78 other occupations (about 400K NYC workers, such as executive assistants, police officers and IT support), most workers nationally hold a degree BLS says isn't needed to start. They're outside the study.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontFamily": "Inter, 'Segoe UI', wf_segoe-ui_normal, helvetica, arial, sans-serif",
                      "fontSize": "8pt",
                      "color": "#1F2328"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
